Package: dh-scala
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 debhelper,
 default-jdk-headless,
 libarchive-zip-perl,
 libdpkg-perl,
 maven-repo-helper,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${perl:Depends},
Provides:
 dh-sequence-scala,
Description: debhelper build system for Scala libraries
 dh-scala builds Scala libraries for Debian without sbt. A short
 debian/scala-build file lists, for each artifact and Scala binary version
 (2.12, 2.13 or 3), the source directories, the compiler options copied from
 upstream's build.sbt and the dependencies, given as Maven coordinates
 resolved in /usr/share/maven-repo. dh-scala compiles the Scala and Java
 sources with the Scala compiler from the archive, writes reproducible jars
 and installs them with maven-repo-helper under their Maven artifact names
 (such as scala-xml_2.13).
 .
 To use it, build-depend on dh-sequence-scala and the Scala compiler
 package, and call "dh $@ --buildsystem=scala" in debian/rules.

Package: dh-make-scala
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ca-certificates,
 dh-scala (= ${source:Version}),
 git,
 libarchive-zip-perl,
 libio-socket-ssl-perl,
 libnet-ssleay-perl,
 libxml-libxml-perl,
 licensecheck,
 xz-utils,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${perl:Depends},
Recommends:
 apt-file,
Description: start Debian packages of Scala libraries from Maven Central
 dh-make-scala writes the debian/ directory of a Scala library, built with
 dh-scala, from what upstream publishes: the POM on Maven Central and the git
 tag of the release. One source package covers every module of the upstream
 repository and every requested Scala binary version (2.12, 2.13, 3), with
 one binary package per module and version. Values it cannot know, such as
 descriptions and copyright holders, are marked for review.
 .
 It can also list which dependencies of a library are missing from Debian
 (estimate), and compare built jars with upstream's, class by class (check).
